      "Language": "eng",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "Neck pain is a common complaint of patients seeking care in the outpatient setting, and the cases seen vary widely in severity and cause. A careful history and physical exam, followed by appropriate imaging studies, are essential for the orderly work-up and management of neck pain in the ambulatory patient. Available imaging studies include plain film radiography, computed tomography (CT), magnetic resonance, and CT myelography. The general considerations necessary to select the appropriate imaging study are discussed for a broad spectrum of common disorders."},
